[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py mis-models the DagEngineLite interface against low/dag_engine_lite.pyi and low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi: the add_node transition (lines 304-306 and its argument domains at 307-311) checks node_is_new only after an arbitrary node_id is drawn and puts no freshness constraint on node_id, so the state machine selects add_node again for an already registered identifier and raises a requirement failure instead of excluding that call, violating the DuplicateNodeError precondition; add_node also admits action through Domain.any() (line 309) even though NodeDefinition.action is contracted as Callable[[], Any]; mark_running, mark_succeeded and mark_failed (lines 508-569) lack the registered-node gate that get_state enforces (lines 582-593), so the model drives these transitions for identifiers not present in the DAG, where marking an unregistered node has no contracted outcome; run (lines 608-664) unconditionally promotes every non-terminal node to SUCCEEDED although the runner contract in low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi requires FAILED results for actions that raise, so subsequent get_state and get_all_states modeled values diverge; and is_finished (lines 571-580) treats a graph whose remaining nodes are blocked by cyclic or missing dependencies as finished, while the impl-level is_finished grounding restricts True to all-terminal, empty, or failed-dependency-blocked graphs. The argument domains and transition state must constrain generation to sequences that satisfy every low-level precondition and must model the same postconditions as the contracted scheduler.
