[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Add deterministic contract-violation and blocked-progress scenarios for the coverage suite: duplicate add_node asserts DuplicateNodeError; unregistered identifiers for add_edge/remove_node/get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents/scheduler get_state assert NodeNotFoundError; validate and DAGRunner.run over an unregistered dependency assert NodeNotFoundError; two-node and self-edge cycles assert CycleError from validate and topological_sort with the contracted cycle sequence asserted; empty-DAG compute_critical_path returns an empty path with zero weight; remove_node purges scheduler tracking for a node already in RUNNING state; mark_succeeded exercises a dependent already past PENDING; mark_failed under CONTINUE_ON_ERROR exercises an independent RUNNING node plus a transitive multi-path dependent; is_finished reports finished when the only non-terminal node is blocked by a failed upstream dependency; and next_wave returns the empty list when remaining nodes have unsatisfied dependencies.
